              }
            ],
            "id": "3402485813",
            "layout": "vertical",
            "purpose": "none",
            "type": "group"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2692577624",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "learnbydoing",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "jx9kbrhzx0p63e9",
                "text": "Concentration Cell"
              }
            ],
            "id": "gqwinxxhhde7sic",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Finally, we take a brief look at a special type of cell called a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "concentration cell"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "An electrochemical cell in which both half-cells consist of the same substances, but the solutions have different concentrations; it has a potential difference and produces current due to the concentration gradient."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2418774638",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1714385138",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ". In a concentration cell, the electrodes are the same material and the half-cells differ only in concentration. Since one or both compartments are not standard, the cell potentials will be unequal; therefore, there will be a potential difference, which can be determined with the aid of the Nernst equation."
              }
            ],
            "id": "vq1v5gxoyolfsnc",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "84541386",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What is the cell potential of the concentration cell described by:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rzi9nmoyed2m7ql",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "n5h6makmgmxgw6y",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "nnvusb4q1wpiafq",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Zn}(s)│\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.10\\;\\mathrm M)║\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.50\\;\\mathrm M)│\\mathrm{Zn}(s)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "From the information given:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "k1dqmxp8thmoxrx",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "bjvrnbl2ld6v3jq",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2i3ogdwfo160si7",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{Anode}:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}(s)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.10\\;\\mathrm M)\\;+\\;2\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;E_\\mathrm{anode}^\\circ\\;\\;=\\;-0.7618\\;\\mathrm V\\\\\\underline{\\mathrm{Cathode}:\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.50\\;\\mathrm M)\\;+\\;2\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}(s)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;E_\\mathrm{cathode}^\\circ=\\;-0.7618\\;\\mathrm V}\\\\\\mathrm{Overall}:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.50\\;\\mathrm M)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}(aq,\\;0.10\\;\\mathrm M)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;E_\\mathrm{cell}^\\circ\\;=\\;0.000\\;\\mathrm V\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The standard cell potential is zero because the anode and cathode involve the same reaction; only the concentration of Zn"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " changes. Substituting into the Nernst equation,"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wu1grhf2e8gu8ih",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "y7c84bcdwxi20wa",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "09i3a1rx6czswj6",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "E_{\\mathrm{cell}}\\;=\\;0.000\\;\\mathrm V\\;-\\frac{\\;0.0592\\;\\mathrm V}2\\;\\log\\;\\left(\\frac{0.10}{0.50}\\right)\\;=\\;+0.021\\;\\mathrm V",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "and the process is spontaneous at these conditions."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "friyzpmsi1mwzvm",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "318285625",
